// W2-UNRUN-2 re-score pin (2026-07-31, in-model CRITICAL, demonstrated
// end-to-end before the fix).
//
// The sibling rows in this directory pin ANONYMOUS Except-carried
// hypothesis binders. This one pins the NAMED spelling of the same
// goal, which EMITTED until 2026-07-31 because gate 3's TEST 1
// exempted every named domain ("a named domain is never a folded
// hypothesis"). That premise was false: the Lean binder name is
// copied from the SAWCore VarName whether or not the Pi is
// dependent, and `parse_core` preserves a hand-written name — so
// naming the binder `h` walked the goal straight past the gate,
// while the printer anonymized the unused name and shipped a bare
// arrow. Gate and artifact disagreed.
//
// It was not a milder spelling. Measured 2026-07-31 at the
// pre-fix HEAD: SAW PROVES the hypothesis (lazy `at`, error slot
// unforced) and REFUTES the conclusion `3 = 4`, so the obligation
// is FALSE; the emitted goal is provable in Lean via
// `congrArg Except.isOk` with `[propext, Quot.sound]` — both on the
// replay allowlist — so `offline_lean_replay` would have issued
// LeanReplayEvidence for a false claim.
//
// FIX: the gate now runs the printer's own `anonymizeUnusedPiBinders`
// before asking TEST 1's anonymity question, so it inspects the
// binders the artifact actually ships.
//
// MUTATION (stated, per rule C4): restore the blanket
// `| Just _ <- mnm = []` in `leanExceptCarriedGoalBinders`, or drop
// the `anonymizeUnusedPiBinders` call in its `goSpine` — either
// turns this row from refusal back to emission.
enable_experimental;
prove_core (do { goal_num_when 0 (offline_lean "named_hyp"); assume_unsat; })
  "(h : EqTrue (bvult 8 (at 2 (Vec 8 Bool) [bvNat 8 7, error (Vec 8 Bool) \"e\"] 0) (bvNat 8 100))) -> EqTrue (bvEq 8 (bvNat 8 3) (bvNat 8 4))";
